      "output": "## Summary\n\nI evaluated `artifacts/data-profile.json` against the `eda` skill's gate thresholds without recomputing anything, and wrote `artifacts/data-gate.md`.\n\n**Result: `GATE: PASS`** \u2014 all 9 checks pass:\n- Null share on all 6 columns: 0.0% (threshold: fail if > 20%)\n- Exact duplicate rows: 0.0% (threshold: fail if > 1%)\n- Key uniqueness on `date`: `unique: true`, 0 duplicates (a real check \u2014 `key_uniqueness.column` was not null)\n- Time coverage: 0 missing days across 1,461/1,461 expected daily periods, 2012-01-01 to 2015-12-31\n\n**Flags carried forward for the analysis step** (none breach a threshold, but affect interpretation):\n- `precipitation` is heavily right-skewed with 14.1% IQR outliers \u2014 report median alongside any mean.\n- `wind` has 2.3% IQR outliers (minor).\n- `precipitation` and `weather` disagree on some rows (all `drizzle`/`fog`/`sun` days show zero precipitation, and 6.9% of `rain` days also show zero) \u2014 don't assume the two columns are always consistent.\n- Units for `wind`, `temp_max`/`temp_min`, `precipitation` are inferred (m/s, \u00b0C, mm), not documented in source.\n- No station/location field confirming this is a single Seattle station.\n\nWrote `artifacts/scratch/gate-checks.csv` and emitted it via `show_table` (9 rows) so the gate decision is made against the actual check table, not the prose.\n\nNo concerns for the next step beyond carrying the flags above as caveats \u2014 the data is clean enough to proceed to analysis.",
